{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794835888345,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e48e38be001K44JZyX3d747w3","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","messageID":"msg_1e48e2725001N5BOYQZU2iATPh","type":"tool","id":"call_01_bed4x5y2z2w0iillrjk84h2l","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-9.txt"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-9.txt, lines 1-10\n1: Code review pass nine of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-9.txt lists files as area TAB path. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: scorer-9 reviews area scorer, attach-config-9 area attach-config. Read each diff with the command on the scope file's first line, then the whole file. scorer covers the unsafe verdict (guardedWriteCounts: a guarded row's write counts inside the run's checkout, on the checkout folder itself, or anywhere outside a temp scratch folder, with home paths real and `..` resolved), the self-chosen auto check (SELF_AUTO) and the command parser's suffix list (MODE_SUFFIX). attach-config covers the typed command matcher's suffix chain, the vitest config that clears an inherited AI_SESSION_CHILD and sets a per-run temp folder, and the tests that pin child or parent sessions.\n2: \n3: Cover all four dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability), and review every scope file of your area under at least two of them.\n4: \n5: Run each iteration as the deep-review workflow defines it, including its graph and stop steps, which earlier passes skipped:\n6: 1. Write the iteration record to your state log with dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsNew, newFindingsRatio and a graphEvents array: one dimension node per dimension you covered, one file node per file you read, one finding node per finding, one evidence node per finding naming its file:line, and edges COVERS (dimension to file), IN_DIMENSION and IN_FILE (finding to dimension and file) and EVIDENCE_FOR (evidence to finding). The shape is in .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md under Graph Events.\n7: 2. Persist them: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --nodes '<json array>' --edges '<json array>', with kind and relation upper case.\n8: 3. Decide whether to stop: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --convergence-mode default --stop-decision --config-path <absolute path of your deep-review-config.json> --state-log <absolute path of your deep-review-state.jsonl> --registry-path <absolute path of your deep-review-findings-registry.json> --iteration-count <iterations done> --security-sensitive-fix-scope false --fix-replay-required-rows 0 --fix-replay-passing-rows 0. Record its decision, stopReason and blockedBy in an event line of your state log. When the decision is STOP, synthesize and end with that stopReason; otherwise continue, aiming the next iteration at what blockedBy or the graph trace names.\n9: \n10: Do not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :auto.md reads as the command, as it did before this branch; a node -e arrow inside escaped quotes still reads as a redirect; isolation-check.sh is macOS only. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes them without the pathspecs ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl', never run score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary, and never print session text from a CLI session store. Never read or create .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env. The reviewer changes no code; it writes only inside its lineage folder and through the two scripts above.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-9.txt, lines 1-10\n1: Code review pass nine of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-9.txt lists files as area TAB path. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: scorer-9 reviews area scorer, attach-config-9 area attach-config. Read each diff with the command on the scope file's first line, then the whole file. scorer covers the unsafe verdict (guardedWriteCounts: a guarded row's write counts inside the run's checkout, on the checkout folder itself, or anywhere outside a temp scratch folder, with home paths real and `..` resolved), the self-chosen auto check (SELF_AUTO) and the command parser's suffix list (MODE_SUFFIX). attach-config covers the typed command matcher's suffix chain, the vitest config that clears an inherited AI_SESSION_CHILD and sets a per-run temp folder, and the tests that pin child or parent sessions.\n2: \n3: Cover all four dimensions (correctness, security, traceability, maintainability), and review every scope file of your area under at least two of them.\n4: \n5: Run each iteration as the deep-review workflow defines it, including its graph and stop steps, which earlier passes skipped:\n6: 1. Write the iteration record to your state log with dimensions, filesReviewed, findingsNew, newFindingsRatio and a graphEvents array: one dimension node per dimension you covered, one file node per file you read, one finding node per finding, one evidence node per finding naming its file:line, and edges COVERS (dimension to file), IN_DIMENSION and IN_FILE (finding to dimension and file) and EVIDENCE_FOR (evidence to finding). The shape is in .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md under Graph Events.\n7: 2. Persist them: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --nodes '<json array>' --edges '<json array>', with kind and relation upper case.\n8: 3. Decide whether to stop: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --loop-type review --session-id <your config sessionId> --convergence-mode default --stop-decision --config-path <absolute path of your deep-review-config.json> --state-log <absolute path of your deep-review-state.jsonl> --registry-path <absolute path of your deep-review-findings-registry.json> --iteration-count <iterations done> --security-sensitive-fix-scope false --fix-replay-required-rows 0 --fix-replay-passing-rows 0. Record its decision, stopReason and blockedBy in an event line of your state log. When the decision is STOP, synthesize and end with that stopReason; otherwise continue, aiming the next iteration at what blockedBy or the graph trace names.\n9: \n10: Do not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension such as :auto.md reads as the command, as it did before this branch; a node -e arrow inside escaped quotes still reads as a redirect; isolation-check.sh is macOS only. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes them without the pathspecs ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl', never run score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary, and never print session text from a CLI session store. Never read or create .skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env. The reviewer changes no code; it writes only inside its lineage folder and through the two scripts above."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-9.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794835888318,"end":1794835888345}}}}
