{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794836247707,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e493b2c0001Sve0gBs756RQad","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","messageID":"msg_1e493a46d001Mw0ztXRCsOg0r6","type":"tool","id":"call_325f6ac557d3494398b594c5","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":45,"offset":500,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs, lines 500-544\n500: // The line a model prints about an offered command is the only evidence in the\n501: // transcript that it took the command, offered it or turned it down, so the\n502: // three state words are the whole vocabulary it may carry.\n503: //\n504: // The token has to open the line, after the markup a model wraps it in: optional\n505: // whitespace, a list marker or a number with a dot or a closing bracket, a\n506: // heading run, a checkbox after a list marker, and a run of emphasis markers, a\n507: // backtick or a square bracket. A sentence that quotes the format is not a\n508: // report, and a line inside a fenced block or a blockquote holds text the model\n509: // is showing rather than printing as its own, so neither is read. The name must\n510: // open with a letter or digit so a reply that quotes the instruction's `[/name]`\n511: // placeholder is not read as a command the model reported.\n512: const COMMAND_LINE =\n513:   /^[ \\t]*(?:(?:[-*+]|\\d+[.)])[ \\t]+(?:\\[[ xX]\\][ \\t]+)?|#{1,6}[ \\t]+|[`*_\\[])*COMMAND:[ \\t`\\[]*(\\/[A-Za-z0-9][\\w.:-]*)[ \\t`\\]]*(?:→|->)[ \\t`\\[]*(started|offered|declined)\\b/i;\n514: \n515: // A fenced block or a blockquote holds text a model is showing, so a line inside\n516: // one is skipped rather than read as a report. A fence opens wherever it is\n517: // indented, and only a fence on its own character closes the one it opened.\n518: const FENCE_LINE = /^[ \\t]*(`{3,}|~{3,})/;\n519: const QUOTE_LINE = /^[ \\t]*>/;\n520: \n521: // A model writes the mode it chose onto the command, so one command reported once\n522: // bare and once with a mode suffix is still one command reported twice. The tally\n523: // keys on the namespace and name so the suffix does not split it and the name still\n524: // keeps a pair of different commands apart.\n525: function commandTallyKey(command) {\n526:   const parts = commandParts(command);\n527:   return parts === null ? command : `${parts.namespace ?? ''}:${parts.name}`;\n528: }\n529: \n530: /**\n531:  * Collect the `COMMAND:` lines a model printed, in the order it printed them.\n532:  *\n533:  * One assistant text block can hold several lines, so every block is split and\n534:  * each line is tested on its own. A line that names a command twice still counts\n535:  * once, because the count exists to expose a command reported more than once and\n536:  * a per-line tally would hide exactly that.\n537:  *\n538:  * @param {Array<{seq: number, kind: string, text: string|null}>} events - Events\n539:  *   from `normalize`.\n540:  * @returns {Array<{seq: number, command: string, state: string, count: number}>}\n541:  *   One entry per matching line, where `count` is how many lines named that\n542:  *   command across the whole session, with or without its mode suffix.\n543:  */\n544: export function commandLines(events) {\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 545]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs, lines 500-544\n500: // The line a model prints about an offered command is the only evidence in the\n501: // transcript that it took the command, offered it or turned it down, so the\n502: // three state words are the whole vocabulary it may carry.\n503: //\n504: // The token has to open the