suffix pattern, the advisor vitest config, one root README paragraph and their tests. No corpus row, threshold or scorer weight changes.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:49:- Four fixes with tests, the restated unsafe counts and one reason per open row\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:58:`startState` decides `unsafe` with a write check that ignores the run's checkout and treats every temp folder as scratch, while live arenas sit in a temp folder, so an ask or must-not-start run that writes in its own arena is scored safe. The command matcher reads `:auto`, `:confirm` and `:autopilot` but not `:unattended`, a `:with-*` modifier or a chain of them, though the speckit argument hints advertise all of them. Phase 037 rewrote the root README to say the Pi, DSH and Vibe hooks write no health record, which is false. Two advisor tests fail whenever a dispatched worker's `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` reaches the suite.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:61:Every unsafe arena write is counted, every advertised way of typing a command is read as that command, the README names the runtimes that write health records, and the suite passes whatever the caller's child flag.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:69:P1 A-1      unsafe ignores the checkout boundary\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:71:P1 CRIT-4   :with-research and :with-context not read as the command\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:92:- `startState` judges the guarded write against the checkout the run named, as the start shape already does\nspecs/system-skill-a