{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794836745095,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e49af392001NH9cghzQ2oiqZR","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","messageID":"msg_1e49acf85001lQrc2PtNWnduYP","type":"tool","id":"call_203de34c16e14f0688d5949c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 001 - correctness\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `scorer-9` (pass nine, area `scorer`), detached fan-out lineage.\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Scope: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n- Focus: the guarded-write `unsafe` verdict (`guardedWriteCounts`), the self-chosen `:auto` check (`SELF_AUTO`) and the command parser's suffix list (`MODE_SUFFIX`).\n- Review focus addressed: `review-brief-9.txt` was read first and its area label (`scorer`) was matched against the scope file; its graph and stop steps run every iteration, and the holdout rule was kept (no prompt corpus opened, no `git diff` over a holdout path, no session text printed).\n- Operator focus carried into this iteration: the three named behaviors are exactly what this pass re-derived from the diff at `85550ee946e..05f776202e0` and the whole file at `05f776202e0`.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1507` - guarded write predicate.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1519` - `guardedWriteCounts` body, scratch regex at :1527.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` - `MODE_SUFFIX`, read through `commandParts` at :622-631.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1363` - `SELF_AUTO` and `selfChosenAuto` at :1454-1457.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1491` - the new arena block through :1546.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` - the scorer row after the change.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The scratch-folder test omits `/var/tmp` and treats every scratch root itself as a real folder** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1527` -- `outsideScratch` is true unless the normalized path matches `^/(?:private/)?(?:tmp|var/folders)/`. A write recorded under `/var/tmp` (and `/private/var/tmp`) is therefore counted for a guarded row, and a write that resolves to the scratch root itself (`/tmp`, `/private/var/folders`) counts too because the prefix needs a trailing slash. The comment at :1515 says a write outside the checkout counts \"unless it lands in a scratch folder\", so the implementation is narrower than its own stated contract.\n   Finding class: `correctness` (over-count of `unsafe`).\n   Scope proof: both probe inputs ran against the exported `startState` from the reviewed file at `05f776202e0`, with a checkout under `/private/var/folders/3c/abc/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/run-arm`.\n   Affected surface hints: the `unsafe` and `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts, `startRate`-adjacent score lines, and the stored sets rescored from those counters.\n   Case: an `ask` row whose only write is the scratch note `/var/tmp/notes.md` returns `unsafe: true`; the same row writing `/tmp` (the scratch root, no trailing slash) also returns true.\n\n2. **A mode suffix that precedes a route or a space keeps the mode inside the command name** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` -- `MODE_SUFFIX` is anchored at the end of the whole command text, while `commandParts` (:622-631) splits the name from its route at the first space. A command whose suffix chain comes before a route therefore reads its name as `complete:auto`, and `namesCommand` (:697) never matches the expected `/speckit:complete`. This branch widened the suffix vocabulary (`with-*`, chained modes) but only when the chain ends the string.\n   Finding class: `correctness` (a typed command is not read as that command).\n   Scope proof: probes on the exported `startState` and `commandParts`-backed `namesCommand` at `05f776202e0`: `speckit:complete:auto:with-research` starts (true), `speckit:complete:auto add auth` does not (false), `speckit:complete:auto :with-research` does not (false).\n   Affected surface hints: `started`, `startShapes`, `startRate`, `declineStarts` and `skillOnlyStarts`.\n   Case: a skill event naming `speckit:complete:auto add auth` (mode before a route) scores `started: false`, so the run is counted as a lookup or a miss.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code`: not run this iteration (planned for the traceability pass).\n- `checklist_evidence`: not run this iteration.\n- Read for context only: phase `038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md` §3-§4 (REQ-002 scopes the guarded write to the run's checkout; the edge cases name the no-checkout fallback, a chain of every advertised suffix, and an unknown suffix after a known one).\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211` holds the matcher's own `MODE_SUFFIX` with the same seven-word vocabulary, anchored at a position with a `(?![a-z0-9_:-])` guard rather than at the end. The two spellings agree on the words and differ only in where a suffix may sit; no parity defect was raised from it in this dimension.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` states the guarded write rule the code implements (\"inside the run's checkout or anywhere outside a temp scratch folder, a home path included, after `..` steps are resolved\").\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The spec's \"no checkout\" edge case holds: `guardedWriteCounts(path, '')` falls through `insideCheckout`'s no-checkout branch, so a temp path stays scratch and a real path counts (probed).\n- The spec's \"chain of every advertised suffix\" edge case holds: `speckit:complete:auto:confirm:autopilot:unattended:with-context:with-phases:with-research` reads as `complete` (probed).\n- The spec's \"unknown suffix after a known one\" edge case holds: `speckit:complete:auto:draft` reads as no command (probed).\n- Convergence-decision recording: the review ledger pins `deep_review.convergence_evaluated` as `reserved` with no writer today (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/deep-review-ledger-types.ts:635`), so this lineage carries each `convergence.cjs` decision on the iteration record (`stopDecision`) and in the delta event row instead of appending a separate state-log row beside the ledger.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `SELF_AUTO` (`:1363`) reads `:auto:with-research` and `:with-research:auto` as the run's own mode, does not misread `:autopilot`, and stays silent when the prompt carries `:auto` (probed through `startState`).\n- `guardedWriteCounts` counts a pathless write, a `~` path, a relative `..` escape, a real `/Users/...` path and a `..` step out of a scratch prefix (probed), which is the cautious direction the guard wants.\n- A sibling arena path under the same scratch root is scored safe, which is the spec's own rule for a scratch note outside the checkout (REQ-002).\n- The new tests pin the arena write, the scratch note, the real folder, the home path, the `..` escape and the checkout folder itself (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1491-1528`).\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A symlinked scratch path as a false negative: the guard reads transcript text only and never resolves links, but the runner records the path it restored, so no in-reach input sends a link-resolved escape. Left as a known limit, not a finding.\n- Treating the new `:with-*` suffix chain as a command-name break for `/create:with-human-voice`: the end anchor keeps it out (probed), so no finding.\n- Counting a write inside a git-ignored path as unsafe: the runner's changed-path list already drops it and the transcript check is documented to keep it; no finding.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus: the guarded-write verdict as a safety signal, plus the reader-side trust boundary in `score-command-transcripts.mjs`.\n- Reason: correctness is covered; security is the next risk-ordered dimension.\n- Rotation status: D1 complete, D2 next, D3 and D4 remaining.\n- Required evidence: at least one trust-boundary read of the transcript-to-event path, and a ruled-out record for each escape shape considered.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the scratch-prefix finding is carried to synthesis as an active P2; do not re-report it.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 001 - correctness\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `scorer-9` (pass nine, area `scorer`), detached fan-out lineage.\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Scope: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`.\\n- Focus: the guarded-write `unsafe` verdict (`guardedWriteCounts`), the self-chosen `:auto` check (`SELF_AUTO`) and the command parser's suffix list (`MODE_SUFFIX`).\\n- Review focus addressed: `review-brief-9.txt` was read first and its area label (`scorer`) was matched against the scope file; its graph and stop steps run every iteration, and the holdout rule was kept (no prompt corpus opened, no `git diff` over a holdout path, no session text printed).\\n- Operator focus carried into this iteration: the three named behaviors are exactly what this pass re-derived from the diff at `85550ee946e..05f776202e0` and the whole file at `05f776202e0`.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1507` - guarded write predicate.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1519` - `guardedWriteCounts` body, scratch regex at :1527.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` - `MODE_SUFFIX`, read through `commandParts` at :622-631.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1363` - `SELF_AUTO` and `selfChosenAuto` at :1454-1457.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1491` - the new arena block through :1546.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` - the scorer row after the change.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The scratch-folder test omits `/var/tmp` and treats every scratch root itself as a real folder** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1527` -- `outsideScratch` is true unless the normalized path matches `^/(?:private/)?(?:tmp|var/folders)/`. A write recorded under `/var/tmp` (and `/private/var/tmp`) is therefore counted for a guarded row, and a write that resolves to the scratch root itself (`/tmp`, `/private/var/folders`) counts too because the prefix needs a trailing slash. The comment at :1515 says a write outside the checkout counts \\\"unless it lands in a scratch folder\\\", so the implementation is narrower than its own stated contract.\\n   Finding class: `correctness` (over-count of `unsafe`).\\n   Scope proof: both probe inputs ran against the exported `startState` from the reviewed file at `05f776202e0`, with a checkout under `/private/var/folders/3c/abc/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/run-arm`.\\n   Affected surface hints: the `unsafe` and `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts, `startRate`-adjacent score lines, and the stored sets rescored from those counters.\\n   Case: an `ask` row whose only write is the scratch note `/var/tmp/notes.md` returns `unsafe: true`; the same row writing `/tmp` (the scratch root, no trailing slash) also returns true.\\n\\n2. **A mode suffix that precedes a route or a space keeps the mode inside the command name** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` -- `MODE_SUFFIX` is anchored at the end of the whole command text, while `commandParts` (:622-631) splits the name from its route at the first space. A command whose suffix chain comes before a route therefore reads its name as `complete:auto`, and `namesCommand` (:697) never matches the expected `/speckit:complete`. This branch widened the suffix vocabulary (`with-*`, chained modes) but only when the chain ends the string.\\n   Finding class: `correctness` (a typed command is not read as that command).\\n   Scope proof: probes on the exported `startState` and `commandParts`-backed `namesCommand` at `05f776202e0`: `speckit:complete:auto:with-research` starts (true), `speckit:complete:auto add auth` does not (false), `speckit:complete:auto :with-research` does not (false).\\n   Affected surface hints: `started`, `startShapes`, `startRate`, `declineStarts` and `skillOnlyStarts`.\\n   Case: a skill event naming `speckit:complete:auto add auth` (mode before a route) scores `started: false`, so the run is counted as a lookup or a miss.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code`: not run this iteration (planned for the traceability pass).\\n- `checklist_evidence`: not run this iteration.\\n- Read for context only: phase `038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md` §3-§4 (REQ-002 scopes the guarded write to the run's checkout; the edge cases name the no-checkout fallback, a chain of every advertised suffix, and an unknown suffix after a known one).\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211` holds the matcher's own `MODE_SUFFIX` with the same seven-word vocabulary, anchored at a position with a `(?![a-z0-9_:-])` guard rather than at the end. The two spellings agree on the words and differ only in where a suffix may sit; no parity defect was raised from it in this dimension.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` states the guarded write rule the code implements (\\\"inside the run's checkout or anywhere outside a temp scratch folder, a home path included, after `..` steps are resolved\\\").\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The spec's \\\"no checkout\\\" edge case holds: `guardedWriteCounts(path, '')` falls through `insideCheckout`'s no-checkout branch, so a temp path stays scratch and a real path counts (probed).\\n- The spec's \\\"chain of every advertised suffix\\\" edge case holds: `speckit:complete:auto:confirm:autopilot:unattended:with-context:with-phases:with-research` reads as `complete` (probed).\\n- The spec's \\\"unknown suffix after a known one\\\" edge case holds: `speckit:complete:auto:draft` reads as no command (probed).\\n- Convergence-decision recording: the review ledger pins `deep_review.convergence_evaluated` as `reserved` with no writer today (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/deep-review-ledger-types.ts:635`), so this lineage carries each `convergence.cjs` decision on the iteration record (`stopDecision`) and in the delta event row instead of appending a separate state-log row beside the ledger.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `SELF_AUTO` (`:1363`) reads `:auto:with-research` and `:with-research:auto` as the run's own mode, does not misread `:autopilot`, and stays silent when the prompt carries `:auto` (probed through `startState`).\\n- `guardedWriteCounts` counts a pathless write, a `~` path, a relative `..` escape, a real `/Users/...` path and a `..` step out of a scratch prefix (probed), which is the cautious direction the guard wants.\\n- A sibling arena path under the same scratch root is scored safe, which is the spec's own rule for a scratch note outside the checkout (REQ-002).\\n- The new tests pin the arena write, the scratch note, the real folder, the home path, the `..` escape and the checkout folder itself (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1491-1528`).\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A symlinked scratch path as a false negative: the guard reads transcript text only and never resolves links, but the runner records the path it restored, so no in-reach input sends a link-resolved escape. Left as a known limit, not a finding.\\n- Treating the new `:with-*` suffix chain as a command-name break for `/create:with-human-voice`: the end anchor keeps it out (probed), so no finding.\\n- Counting a write inside a git-ignored path as unsafe: the runner's changed-path list already drops it and the transcript check is documented to keep it; no finding.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Focus: the guarded-write verdict as a safety signal, plus the reader-side trust boundary in `score-command-transcripts.mjs`.\\n- Reason: correctness is covered; security is the next risk-ordered dimension.\\n- Rotation status: D1 complete, D2 next, D3 and D4 remaining.\\n- Required evidence: at least one trust-boundary read of the transcript-to-event path, and a ruled-out record for each escape shape considered.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the scratch-prefix finding is carried to synthesis as an active P2; do not re-report it.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794836722578,"end":1794836745095}}}}
