{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794836906853,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e49dc1c6001WmntZ9Vi21Yo25","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","messageID":"msg_1e49db80a001yBx8CcP6zUXaYp","type":"tool","id":"call_466464873c6c4de8b1166c6c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-165\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - scorer-9\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: Pass-nine fan-out lineage for the `scorer` area. Reviews the command-transcript scorer,\n6: its vitest file and its README row: the guarded-write `unsafe` verdict, the self-chosen\n7: `:auto` check (`SELF_AUTO`) and the command parser's mode suffix list (`MODE_SUFFIX`).\n8: \n9: ## 2. TOPIC\n10: \n11: Review: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build (lineage scorer-9, pass 9)\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n16: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n17: - [ ] security\n18: - [ ] traceability\n19: - [ ] maintainability\n20: \n21: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n22: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n23: \n24: - The `attach-config` area: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`,\n25:   `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `vitest.config.ts`, `tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts`.\n26: - Rescoring stored sets, changing thresholds, weights or corpus rows.\n27: - Reading holdout or prompt corpora; printing session text from a CLI session store.\n28: - Changing code under review. This lineage reports findings only.\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n33: \n34: - Convergence at the configured threshold (0.10) once every dimension is covered.\n35: - `maxIterations` 8.\n36: - Any active P0 stops a PASS verdict regardless of convergence.\n37: \n38: ---\n39: \n40: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n41: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n42: - [x] correctness\n43: \n44: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n45: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n46: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n47: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n48: - P1 (Required): 0\n49: - P2 (Suggestions): 2\n50: - Resolved: 0\n51: \n52: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n53: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n54: \n55: - Reading the committed spec phase `038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md` beside the diff\n56:   named what each changed line is for (iteration 1).\n57: \n58: ---\n59: \n60: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n61: \n62: - [First iteration -- populated as each iteration records a failed approach]\n63: \n64: ---\n65: \n66: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n67: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n68: ### A symlinked scratch path as a false negative: the guard reads transcript text only and never resolves links, but the runner records the path it restored, so no in-reach input sends a link-resolved escape. Left as a known limit, not a finding. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n69: - What was tried: A symlinked scratch path as a false negative: the guard reads transcript text only and never resolves links, but the runner records the path it restored, so no in-reach input sends a link-resolved escape. Left as a known limit, not a finding.\n70: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n71: - Do NOT retry: A symlinked scratch path as a false negative: the guard reads transcript text only and never resolves links, but the runner records the path it restored, so no in-reach input sends a link-resolved escape. Left as a known limit, not a finding.\n72: \n73: ### Counting a write inside a git-ignored path as unsafe: the runner's changed-path list already drops it and the transcript check is documented to keep it; no finding. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n74: - What was tried: Counting a write inside a git-ignored path as unsafe: the runner's changed-path list already drops it and the transcript check is documented to keep it; no finding.\n75: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n76: - Do NOT retry: Counting a write inside a git-ignored path as unsafe: the runner's changed-path list already drops it and the transcript check is documented to keep it; no finding.\n77: \n78: ### Treating the new `:with-*` suffix chain as a command-name break for `/create:with-human-voice`: the end anchor keeps it out (probed), so no finding. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n79: - What was tried: Treating the new `:with-*` suffix chain as a command-name break for `/create:with-human-voice`: the end anchor keeps it out (probed), so no finding.\n80: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n81: - Do NOT retry: Treating the new `:with-*` suffix chain as a command-name break for `/create:with-human-voice`: the end anchor keeps it out (probed), so no finding.\n82: \n83: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n84: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n85: - Completed pivots: 0\n86: - Failed pivots: 0\n87: - Audited overrides: 0\n88: - Swept: none yet\n89: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n90: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n91: \n92: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n93: \n94: - A symlinked scratch path as a false negative: the guard reads transcript text only and never resolves links, so no in-reach input sends a link-resolved escape (iteration 1).\n95: - A `:with-*` chain breaking `/create:with-human-voice`: the end anchor keeps it out (iteration 1, probed).\n96: - A git-ignored write counting as unsafe: the changed-path list already drops it and the transcript check is documented to keep it (iteration 1).\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n101: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n102: - Dimension: security - Focus: the guarded-write verdict as a safety signal, plus the reader-side trust boundary in `score-command-transcripts.mjs`. - Reason: correctness is covered; security is the next risk-ordered dimension. - Rotation status: D1 complete, D2 next, D3 and D4 remaining. - Required evidence: at least one trust-boundary read of the transcript-to-event path, and a ruled-out record for each escape shape considered. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: the scratch-prefix finding is carried to synthesis as an active P2; do not re-report it. Review verdict: PASS\n103: \n104: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n105: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n106: \n107: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n108: \n109: - Target pointers: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`\n110:   (guarded write verdict at 1507-1529, self-auto at 1359-1364 and 1454-1457, mode suffix at 610-631),\n111:   `runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n112: - Behavior claims: phase `038-alignment-p1-remediation` REQ-002 (a guarded row writing inside its\n113:   arena checkout is unsafe, a scratch note outside it is not), SC-001 (the arena tests fail on the\n114:   old rule), and the spec edge cases (no-checkout fallback, a chain of every advertised suffix,\n115:   an unknown suffix after a known one).\n116: - Reuse and conventions: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`\n117:   holds the matcher's own suffix chain; the advertised vocabulary is `:auto`, `:confirm`,\n118:   `:autopilot`, `:unattended`, `:with-context`, `:with-phases`, `:with-research`\n119:   (`speckit/README.txt`).\n120: - Review risks and gaps: no `resource-map.md` in the packet; the scorer's behavior is a\n121:   measurement, not runtime enforcement, so severity is judged on measurement fidelity.\n122: \n123: ---\n124: \n125: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n126: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n127: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n128: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n129: | `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n130: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n131: | `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | - | Target is a runtime script, not a skill contract |\n132: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No agent definition changed |\n133: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No catalog row names this script |\n134: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No playbook claim covers the scorer |\n135: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n140: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n141: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n142: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n143: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | D1 | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 2 P2 | partial |\n144: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | D1 | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n145: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` | D1 | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n146: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n147: \n148: ---\n149: \n150: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n151: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n152: - Max iterations: 8\n153: - Convergence threshold: 0.10\n154: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n155: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n156: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n157: - Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-scorer-9-1794835877856-5ghgm4, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n158: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n159: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n160: - Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n161: - Severity threshold: P2\n162: - Review target type: spec-folder\n163: - Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, pl