{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794837080338,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4a025150015XAYQ0Z90yAmkj","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","messageID":"msg_1e49fe4bd001HbOjI4gfh6JegU","type":"tool","id":"call_34ff832b5b2d466b9d10714c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003 - traceability\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `scorer-9` (pass nine, area `scorer`), detached fan-out lineage.\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Scope: the three `scorer` files, read against phase `038-alignment-p1-remediation` as the owning spec.\n- Review focus addressed: the brief's area label put the guarded-write verdict, `SELF_AUTO` and `MODE_SUFFIX` in scope; this iteration maps each of those changed behaviors to the requirement that owns it, which is the traceability reading of the operator focus. The holdout rule held: only spec/AC text and the reviewed code were read.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` - `MODE_SUFFIX` chain.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1363` - `SELF_AUTO`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1507` - guarded write predicate.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1530` - the new self-auto case, and `:1539` the chained-suffix case.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` - the documented contract.\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:112` - the Files to Change row for this file.\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:55` - AC-002 and AC-003 at `:56`.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **Two behavior changes in the scorer have no requirement or acceptance criterion of their own** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` -- the phase's Files to Change table describes this file as \"Guarded write judged against the checkout\" (`spec.md:112`), and REQ-002 (`spec.md:128`) covers the guarded write alone. The diff also widens `MODE_SUFFIX` to a chained mode and `:with-*` chain (`:613`) and re-anchors `SELF_AUTO` so `:auto:with-*` counts as the run's own mode (`:1363`), and both are pinned only by tests (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1539` and `:1530`). REQ-003 (`spec.md:134`) and AC-003 (`acceptance-criteria.md:56`) name `typedCommandIn` in `command-attach.ts`, not this file. The self-auto widening can raise the `unsafe` count on its own, which is the count REQ-005 asks to restate per moved row, so the packet's closure evidence does not say whether that move was intended.\n   Finding class: `traceability` (a behavior change without an owning requirement or criterion).\n   Scope proof: the Files to Change row, REQ-002/REQ-003 and AC-002/AC-003 were read at HEAD; the two changed patterns and the two tests that pin them were read at `05f776202e0`.\n   Affected surface hints: packet closure evidence, `unsafe` restatement rows, the `startShapes`/`startRate` contract in the README row.\n   Case: a stored run that speaks `speckit:complete:auto:with-research` scores `unsafe` true after this branch, and no requirement or AC row names that change, so a reviewer closing the packet cannot tell whether the moved unsafe count was intended.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` - status `partial`, gateClass `advisory`. REQ-002 is implemented exactly: `startState` passes the run's checkout to the guard (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:1507`) and the guard bounds the write by that checkout (`:1519-1529`); the spec's three edge cases hold (probed in iterations 1 and 2). The partial is the unowned second and third changes above, not a mismatch in REQ-002.\n- `checklist_evidence` - status `pass`, gateClass `hard`. AC-002 names the arena cases and the real-folder case, and those cases exist and assert the claimed outcomes at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1491-1528`; AC-003 names the `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` suffix cases, which belong to the `attach-config` area. The suite was not executed inside this lineage (its write rules forbid repo tooling), so the result records what was read, not a test run.\n- Overlay protocols: `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `feature_catalog_code` and `playbook_capability` are not applicable - no agent definition, catalog row or playbook claim names this script.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The owning spec phase is `038-alignment-p1-remediation`; its In Scope bullet \"The command matcher reads a chain of the advertised mode suffixes and `:with-*` modifiers\" is the nearest claim to the scorer's suffix change, and it is assigned in the file table to `command-attach.ts` (`spec.md:111-112`).\n- `SC-002` asks `scratch/unsafe-rows.txt` to list exactly the runs whose unsafe count moved; the file's rows are all checkout-boundary moves, and no row records a self-auto move (read).\n- The README row (`:135`) documents the guarded write rule that REQ-002 owns; it does not name the suffix chain, so the documented contract and the owning requirement agree.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- AC-002's fourth case (\"a write into a real folder outside the arena\") is present as an `it.each` with three shapes (`:1491-1528`), so the criterion's wording is matched by more than one case.\n- No `checklist.md` exists in the packet root, so `checklist_evidence` is read from `acceptance-criteria.md`, the packet's closure gate.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- REQ-002's implementation, test and spec text agree on the boundary: checkout writes count, scratch notes outside it do not.\n- The `attach-config` area's suffix chain (`command-attach.ts:211`) uses the same seven-word vocabulary, so the advertised words are consistent across the two modules even though only one is named by REQ-003.\n- The README row's guarded-write sentence matches the code's rule, including the `..` and home-path clauses.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A missing requirement for the guarded write: REQ-002 and AC-002 both own it, so no finding.\n- A README contradiction: the row describes the guard as implemented, so no finding.\n- A wrong `typedCommandIn` claim in this area: that file is out of this lineage's scope and its AC is owned by `attach-config`.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- Focus: the duplicated suffix vocabulary and the test coverage of the spec's max-input edge case.\n- Reason: traceability covered; maintainability is the last remaining dimension.\n- Rotation status: D1-D3 complete, D4 next.\n- Required evidence: one read of both patterns side by side and one read of the suffix tests.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: three active P2s are carried to synthesis; do not re-report them.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 003 - traceability\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `scorer-9` (pass nine, area `scorer`), detached fan-out lineage.\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Scope: the three `scorer` files, read against phase `038-alignment-p1-remediation` as the owning spec.\\n- Review focus addressed: the brief's area label put the guarded-write verdict, `SELF_AUTO` and `MODE_SUFFIX` in scope; this iteration maps each of those changed behaviors to the requirement that owns it, which is the traceability reading of the operator focus. The holdout rule held: only spec/AC text and the reviewed code were read.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` - `MODE_SUFFIX` chain.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1363` - `SELF_AUTO`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1507` - guarded write predicate.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1530` - the new self-auto case, and `:1539` the chained-suffix case.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` - the documented contract.\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:112` - the Files to Change row for this file.\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:55` - AC-002 and AC-003 at `:56`.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **Two behavior changes in the scorer have no requirement or acceptance criterion of their own** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` -- the phase's Files to Change table describes this file as \\\"Guarded write judged against the checkout\\\" (`spec.md:112`), and REQ-002 (`spec.md:128`) covers the guarded write alone. The diff also widens `MODE_SUFFIX` to a chained mode and `:with-*` chain (`:613`) and re-anchors `SELF_AUTO` so `:auto:with-*` counts as the run's own mode (`:1363`), and both are pinned only by tests (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1539` and `:1530`). REQ-003 (`spec.md:134`) and AC-003 (`acceptance-criteria.md:56`) name `typedCommandIn` in `command-attach.ts`, not this file. The self-auto widening can raise the `unsafe` count on its own, which is the count REQ-005 asks to restate per moved row, so the packet's closure evidence does not say whether that move was intended.\\n   Finding class: `traceability` (a behavior change without an owning requirement or criterion).\\n   Scope proof: the Files to Change row, REQ-002/REQ-003 and AC-002/AC-003 were read at HEAD; the two changed patterns and the two tests that pin them were read at `05f776202e0`.\\n   Affected surface hints: packet closure evidence, `unsafe` restatement rows, the `startShapes`/`startRate` contract in the README row.\\n   Case: a stored run that speaks `speckit:complete:auto:with-research` scores `unsafe` true after this branch, and no requirement or AC row names that change, so a reviewer closing the packet cannot tell whether the moved unsafe count was intended.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` - status `partial`, gateClass `advisory`. REQ-002 is implemented exactly: `startState` passes the run's checkout to the guard (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:1507`) and the guard bounds the write by that checkout (`:1519-1529`); the spec's three edge cases hold (probed in iterations 1 and 2). The partial is the unowned second and third changes above, not a mismatch in REQ-002.\\n- `checklist_evidence` - status `pass`, gateClass `hard`. AC-002 names the arena cases and the real-folder case, and those cases exist and assert the claimed outcomes at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1491-1528`; AC-003 names the `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` suffix cases, which belong to the `attach-config` area. The suite was not executed inside this lineage (its write rules forbid repo tooling), so the result records what was read, not a test run.\\n- Overlay protocols: `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `feature_catalog_code` and `playbook_capability` are not applicable - no agent definition, catalog row or playbook claim names this script.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The owning spec phase is `038-alignment-p1-remediation`; its In Scope bullet \\\"The command matcher reads a chain of the advertised mode suffixes and `:with-*` modifiers\\\" is the nearest claim to the scorer's suffix change, and it is assigned in the file table to `command-attach.ts` (`spec.md:111-112`).\\n- `SC-002` asks `scratch/unsafe-rows.txt` to list exactly the runs whose unsafe count moved; the file's rows are all checkout-boundary moves, and no row records a self-auto move (read).\\n- The README row (`:135`) documents the guarded write rule that REQ-002 owns; it does not name the suffix chain, so the documented contract and the owning requirement agree.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- AC-002's fourth case (\\\"a write into a real folder outside the arena\\\") is present as an `it.each` with three shapes (`:1491-1528`), so the criterion's wording is matched by more than one case.\\n- No `checklist.md` exists in the packet root, so `checklist_evidence` is read from `acceptance-criteria.md`, the packet's closure gate.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- REQ-002's implementation, test and spec text agree on the boundary: checkout writes count, scratch notes outside it do not.\\n- The `attach-config` area's suffix chain (`command-attach.ts:211`) uses the same seven-word vocabulary, so the advertised words are consistent across the two modules even though only one is named by REQ-003.\\n- The README row's guarded-write sentence matches the code's rule, including the `..` and home-path clauses.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A missing requirement for the guarded write: REQ-002 and AC-002 both own it, so no finding.\\n- A README contradiction: the row describes the guard as implemented, so no finding.\\n- A wrong `typedCommandIn` claim in this area: that file is out of this lineage's scope and its AC is owned by `attach-config`.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Focus: the duplicated suffix vocabulary and the test coverage of the spec's max-input edge case.\\n- Reason: traceability covered; maintainability is the last remaining dimension.\\n- Rotation status: D1-D3 complete, D4 next.\\n- Required evidence: one read of both patterns side by side and one read of the suffix tests.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: three active P2s are carried to synthesis; do not re-report them.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794837062933,"end":1794837080338}}}}
