{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794837172435,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4a19f93001n90C49sAJC4bCR","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffe1Z7OkhaCysQjW9","messageID":"msg_1e4a18b84001l9ydiZof9GfVoY","type":"tool","id":"call_e7d3c8c5856e40d08b257f7c","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004 - maintainability\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `scorer-9` (pass nine, area `scorer`), detached fan-out lineage.\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Scope: the three `scorer` files.\n- Review focus addressed: the brief names the suffix list as one of this area's three behaviors; this iteration reads its shape and its test net, which is the maintainability reading of the operator focus. The holdout rule held: only the reviewed files and the spec text were read.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` - `MODE_SUFFIX` vocabulary.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1363` - `SELF_AUTO` vocabulary.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:621` - `commandParts` comment and split.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1531` - the only chained-suffix case, and `:1540` its twin.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` - the row that carries the contract in prose.\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:186` - the max-input edge case.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The advertised suffix vocabulary is duplicated in two patterns and the spec's max-input case is untested** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` -- the seven-word alternation lives in `MODE_SUFFIX` (`:613`) and again in `SELF_AUTO`'s lookahead (`:1363`), and a third copy sits in the matcher (`command-attach.ts:211`). The two copies here serve different anchors, so a new advertised modifier has to be added to both by hand; missing one is silent: the command stops reading as itself at `commandParts` while `SELF_AUTO` still reads it, or the reverse. The test file exercises only `:auto:with-research` (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1531`, `:1540`) and never `:unattended`, `:with-context`, `:with-phases` or the spec's \"a chain of every advertised suffix\" case (`spec.md:186`).\n   Finding class: `maintainability` (duplicated closed vocabulary and an unpinned spec edge case).\n   Scope proof: both patterns were read at `05f776202e0`; the test file's only `with-*` occurrences are the two lines named; the spec's max-input edge case is at `spec.md:186`.\n   Affected surface hints: `commandParts`, `namesCommand`, `confirmStem`, `selfChosenAuto`, and the suffix cases owned by `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`.\n   Case: adding `:with-evidence` to the advertised hints without editing `:613` makes `speckit:complete:auto:with-evidence` read as the command name `complete:auto:with-evidence`, so the start is lost and no test fails.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- No new protocol result this iteration; `spec_code` stays `partial` and `checklist_evidence` stays `pass` from iteration 3. The max-input edge case read here supports the `spec_code` partial rather than raising it.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `command-attach.ts:211` keeps the same seven words with a position guard, so the vocabulary is one contract spread across two modules with no shared constant.\n- The README row (`:135`) states the guarded write rule but does not name the suffix vocabulary, so the only written definition is the two regexes and the command READMEs.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- A chain of every advertised suffix reads correctly today (probed in iteration 1), so the finding is about the cost of the next edit and the missing regression pin, not a live mis-read.\n- `:with-human-voice` is a real command name, and both copies correctly keep it out, so a shared constant would still need the same anchor distinction.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The two patterns agree on the vocabulary as of this commit; no live drift.\n- Each pattern carries a comment naming why its anchor is where it is (`:610-612`, `:1359-1362`), so the intent is documented even though the words are repeated.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Extracting one shared regex across both modules: the anchors differ (end-strip vs lookahead) and the third copy lives in another module, so a shared constant would couple them for one word list. Recorded as a trade-off, not a finding beyond the P2.\n- A missing comment on the new chain: both changed patterns already carry one.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: cross-reference (no dimension remains)\n- Focus: re-read the four findings against the final state and confirm no new defect before synthesis.\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered; the next pass is the convergence confirmation.\n- Rotation status: D1-D4 complete.\n- Required evidence: a bounded re-read of the four cited lines and the AC rows they touch.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: four active P2s are carried to synthesis; do not re-report them.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004 - maintainability\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `scorer-9` (pass nine, area `scorer`), detached fan-out lineage.\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Scope: the three `scorer` files.\\n- Review focus addressed: the brief names the suffix list as one of this area's three behaviors; this iteration reads its shape and its test net, which is the maintainability reading of the operator focus. The holdout rule held: only the reviewed files and the spec text were read.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` - `MODE_SUFFIX` vocabulary.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1363` - `SELF_AUTO` vocabulary.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:621` - `commandParts` comment and split.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1531` - the only chained-suffix case, and `:1540` its twin.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:135` - the row that carries the contract in prose.\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md:186` - the max-input edge case.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The advertised suffix vocabulary is duplicated in two patterns and the spec's max-input case is untested** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:613` -- the seven-word alternation lives in `MODE_SUFFIX` (`:613`) and again in `SELF_AUTO`'s lookahead (`:1363`), and a third copy sits in the matcher (`command-attach.ts:211`). The two copies here serve different anchors, so a new advertised modifier has to be added to both by hand; missing one is silent: the command stops reading as itself at `commandParts` while `SELF_AUTO` still reads it, or the reverse. The test file exercises only `:auto:with-research` (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:1531`, `:1540`) and never `:unattended`, `:with-context`, `:with-phases` or the spec's \\\"a chain of every advertised suffix\\\" case (`spec.md:186`).\\n   Finding class: `maintainability` (duplicated closed vocabulary and an unpinned spec edge case).\\n   Scope proof: both patterns were read at `05f776202e0`; the test file's only `with-*` occurrences are the two lines named; the spec's max-input edge case is at `spec.md:186`.\\n   Affected surface hints: `commandParts`, `namesCommand`, `confirmStem`, `selfChosenAuto`, and the suffix cases owned by `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`.\\n   Case: adding `:with-evidence` to the advertised hints without editing `:613` makes `speckit:complete:auto:with-evidence` read as the command name `complete:auto:with-evidence`, so the start is lost and no test fails.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- No new protocol result this iteration; `spec_code` stays `partial` and `checklist_evidence` stays `pass` from iteration 3. The max-input edge case read here supports the `spec_code` partial rather than raising it.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `command-attach.ts:211` keeps the same seven words with a position guard, so the vocabulary is one contract spread across two modules with no shared constant.\\n- The README row (`:135`) states the guarded write rule but does not name the suffix vocabulary, so the only written definition is the two regexes and the command READMEs.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- A chain of every advertised suffix reads correctly today (probed in iteration 1), so the finding is about the cost of the next edit and the missing regression pin, not a live mis-read.\\n- `:with-human-voice` is a real command name, and both copies correctly keep it out, so a shared constant would still need the same anchor distinction.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The two patterns agree on the vocabulary as of this commit; no live drift.\\n- Each pattern carries a comment naming why its anchor is where it is (`:610-612`, `:1359-1362`), so the intent is documented even though the words are repeated.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Extracting one shared regex across both modules: the anchors differ (end-strip vs lookahead) and the third copy lives in another module, so a shared constant would couple them for one word list. Recorded as a trade-off, not a finding beyond the P2.\\n- A missing comment on the new chain: both changed patterns already carry one.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: cross-reference (no dimension remains)\\n- Focus: re-read the four findings against the final state and confirm no new defect before synthesis.\\n- Reason: all four dimensions are covered; the next pass is the convergence confirmation.\\n- Rotation status: D1-D4 complete.\\n- Required evidence: a bounded re-read of the four cited lines and the AC rows they touch.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: four active P2s are carried to synthesis; do not re-report them.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-9/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794837159827,"end":1794837172435}}}}
